.TH IMPROV-ADD-DERIVED 1 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv\-add\-derived \- Add a derived (formula) measure
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimprov add\-derived\fR <db> <id> <name> <formula>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a derived (formula) measure.
.PP
The formula is the right\-hand side only, e.g. "Price * Quantity" or "SUM(Revenue OVER Time)", with names resolved against the model. The measure\*(Aqs categories come from the measures it references. A formula cycle is refused.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIdb\fR>
The model store: a file, or postgres://USER@HOST/DB?model=NAME
.TP
<\fIid\fR>
The measure\*(Aqs numeric id
.TP
<\fIname\fR>
The measure\*(Aqs name
.TP
<\fIformula\fR>
The formula text (in IMPROV_LOCALE\*(Aqs spelling)
